{"packet_id":"478b8283edfbe4c7","dimensions":{"problem_framing":{"status":"scored","score":1,"event_ids":["A1"],"reason":"A1 restates the question, then lists 'constraints' ('No expansion into new markets or product lines...', 'No new customer groups or routes to reach them') that no dossier source states. These constraints forbid the very option the question asks about. Four of the five alternatives are rewordings of 'do nothing'. The only substantive option, 'personal safety devices', is obvious. A1 does correctly label the budget and timeline as analyst assumptions. It does not separate the objective from a suggested solution, and it does not correct a premise."},"causal_mechanism":{"status":"scored","score":1,"event_ids":["A4","A6"],"reason":"The best theory, T1 (A4), says individuals lack CO awareness and so do not buy alarms. That names a barrier and a revenue benefit. However, value capture is asserted as 'Increased sales of CO alarms would generate revenue for Dr\u00e4gerwerk' without explaining why buyers would choose a differentiated Dr\u00e4ger product over existing detectors. No source shows Dr\u00e4ger sells consumer CO alarms. The chain from behaviour change to value this manufacturer captures is missing."},"distinct_theories":{"status":"scored","score":1,"event_ids":["A4","A6"],"reason":"T2 (A6) copies T1 (A4) word for word and adds 'a lack of legal requirements'. This is an extension of one idea, not a rival explanation. Neither theory implies a different product, customer or channel."},"assumptions_predictions":{"status":"scored","score":1,"event_ids":["A4","A6"],"reason":"Assumptions are stated, such as 'Individuals are not aware of the risks' and 'no legal requirements'. The prediction 'Increased sales... would be observed if individuals are made aware' is vague: it has no magnitude, no population, and no link to Dr\u00e4ger's own sales. It is weakly observable and would not put the theory in clear trouble if it failed. The legal-requirement assumption is never checked, even though A5 retrieved a source labelled draeger-wa-co-law; that source's content is not in the packet."},"evidence_judgement":{"status":"scored","score":1,"event_ids":["A7"],"reason":"A7 quotes draeger-baltimore-co exactly, but labels it 'independent_study' when the dossier class is verified_observation. A7 treats the source as supporting all of T1, including Dr\u00e4ger revenue, yet the source supports only the low knowledge and ownership assumptions. The 'Does not show' note is beside the point. It omits the source's place (Baltimore), its date, its fit with any target customer group, and its silence on willingness to pay for a differentiated product. The draeger-bgr-amazon-co source (cheap, popular, unregulated detectors) and the company-claim division figures are never assessed."},"seeking_challenge":{"status":"not_reached","score":null,"event_ids":["A5","A8"],"reason":"The only later search (A5) looks for confirming awareness evidence. The run stopped at A8 before any disconfirming search would have been expected, so this stage is not reached rather than skipped."},"experiment_design":{"status":"not_reached","score":null,"event_ids":["A8"],"reason":"No test was proposed or declined before the context-limit stop at A8."},"revision":{"status":"not_reached","score":null,"event_ids":["A8"],"reason":"A scheduled update applied (scheduled_update true) but was never delivered (update_delivered false), and the run stopped at A8."},"recommendation":{"status":"not_reached","score":null,"event_ids":["A8"],"reason":"A8: 'The investigation stopped before a recommendation (context limit).'"}},"red_flags":[{"kind":"incomplete","event_ids":["A8"],"reason":"The episode ended before a recommendation, so there is no completed investigation."},{"kind":"unsupported_inference","event_ids":["A4","A6","A7"],"reason":"The theories assert that awareness campaigns would raise CO alarm revenue for Dr\u00e4ger. No source shows Dr\u00e4ger sells consumer CO alarms